# Database Schema Analysis for Timer Sync - UPDATED

## Tables Found
- timer_states: Stores timer state per user (snake_case)
- user_devices: Stores device information and APNs tokens (snake_case)
- users: User accounts
- user_preferences: User preferences
- Other system tables...

## TimerStates Table Structure (based on entity)
- user_id: UUID primary key (one state per user)
- phase: String (work, break, long_break)
- remaining_seconds: Integer
- running: Boolean
- work_duration_minutes: Integer
- break_duration_minutes: Integer
- long_break_duration_minutes: Integer
- auto_start_next: Boolean
- short_breaks_completed: Integer
- last_updated_at: Instant
- updated_by_device_id: UUID (nullable)
- version: Long (for optimistic locking)

## UserDevices Table Structure (based on entity)
- id: UUID primary key
- user_id: UUID foreign key to users
- device_id: String (unique per device)
- device_name: String
- device_type: String (iOS, macOS, watchOS)
- apns_token: String (nullable)
- active: Boolean
- created_at, updated_at: Timestamps

